menu "Esp Talkie Configuration"

    config LED_GPIO
        int "LED GPIO number"
        range 0 33
        default 2
        help
            GPIO number (IOxx) of the LED that shows the push button level
            received from the other boards. The LED turns on while a remote
            push button is pressed.

            The default (GPIO 2) is the on-board LED of most ESP32 DevKit
            boards.

    config PUSH_BUTTON_GPIO
        int "Push button GPIO number"
        range 0 33
        default 22
        help
            GPIO number (IOxx) of the push button. The pin is configured as
            an input with the internal pull-up enabled, so wire the button
            between this GPIO and GND (pressed = low level).

            GPIOs 34-39 are input-only and have no internal pull-up, so they
            are not allowed here.

    menu "Radio Communication"

        config RADIO_COMM_CHANNEL
            int "Wi-Fi channel"
            range 1 14
            default 1
            help
                Wi-Fi channel that ESP-NOW uses to send and receive packets.

                All boards must use the same channel, or they will not hear
                each other. Channels 12-14 are not allowed in every country,
                so check your local regulations before using them.

        config RADIO_COMM_QUEUE_SIZE
            int "Receive queue size"
            range 2 20
            default 6
            help
                Maximum number of received packets waiting to be processed.

                The ESP-NOW receive callback places each valid packet in this
                queue, and the radio_comm task takes them out and dispatches
                them. When the queue is full, new packets are discarded.
                A larger queue tolerates bursts better, at the cost of RAM.

        config RADIO_COMM_MAGIC_NUMBER
            hex "Packet magic number"
            range 0x0000 0xFFFF
            default 0xABDC
            help
                16-bit value sent at the start of every packet header. When a
                packet arrives with a different value, the receiver discards
                it, which filters out ESP-NOW traffic from other applications
                on the same channel.

                All boards must use the same value. Prefer a value whose two
                bytes are different (e.g. 0xABDC instead of 0xAAAA), so that
                byte-order mistakes are detected instead of passing silently.
        
        config RADIO_COMM_PMK
            string "ESPNOW primary master key"
            default "pmk1234567890123"
            help
                ESPNOW primary master for the example to use. The length of ESPNOW primary master must be 16 bytes.

        config RADIO_COMM_LMK
            string "ESPNOW local master key"
            default "lmk1234567890123"
            help
                ESPNOW local master for the example to use. The length of ESPNOW local master must be 16 bytes.

    endmenu

endmenu
